          <li><strong>Qualifies the caller by your rules.</strong> You decide what every caller is asked, which calls book, and which calls go to a person you name. The setup does not add a question you did not approve.</li>
          <li><strong>Books onto your real calendar.</strong> A qualified caller gets a real slot on the calendar you already use, not a message you retype in the morning. It does not invent an open slot. The calendar layer, separate from the phone, is the <a class="text-link" href="/booking-software/">booking software</a> setup.</li>
          <li><strong>Runs the SMS chain.</strong> A confirmation and the next-step text go out after the call. A reply stays inside the rules you approved. Every call is recorded and transcribed so you can review what was said.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          The difference from a traditional answering service is the booking
          step, then the text. A traditional service takes a message and hands
          the work back to you. This setup finishes the booking during the call
          when the rules say to book, then continues by SMS. A call that should
          not be booked takes the message you defined. It does not force a slot.
        </p>

